    {"type":"line","id":"div4","x":40,"y":1645,"width":1560,"height":0,"points":[[0,0],[1560,0]],"strokeColor":"#64748b","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"seed":256022},
    {"type":"text","id":"pat_h","x":40,"y":1660,"width":400,"height":15,"strokeColor":"#93c5fd","text":"PATTERNS IT INSTANCES","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":257001},
    {"type":"text","id":"pat_t","x":40,"y":1682,"width":1560,"height":45,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"[16] The Permission Ladder: every command is printed for an operator, never run — a command that discards work goes out on the ask rung with no deny and no warning\n[17] Blast-Radius Gating: meant to prepare the way back before a risky change; the way back is written before the change is known\n[19] Scope Lock and Checkpoint Delivery: one plan per locked workstream, and the TLS plan answers the sprint's TLS-stability trigger","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":257002},
    {"type":"text","id":"missing","x":40,"y":1745,"width":1560,"height":45,"strokeColor":"#fecaca","text":"deliberately missing: a plan derived from the change (a git diff from the sprint's starting commit: committed files want a revert, uncommitted ones a warning)\n· a deny on discarding (print the checkout only after confirming no uncommitted edits, or not at all) · being called (a phase that runs it before a risky change)\n· in the prototype: no state file is read, no cluster commands are printed, and the load-failure path is described rather than reproduced","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":257003}
  ],
